[size=5][b]Why SkTestLab?[/b][/size]

A successful reload is a useful start. Repeatable tests help you check the behavior behind your scripts: reward calculations, boundary values, expected failures, and the functions you change most often.

Keep [b].sk[/b] files and [b].sktest.json[/b] tests together in your project. Run a check from VS Code's native Test Explorer, inspect the evidence, and rerun failures while you work.

[size=5][b]A complete testing workflow[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Source diagnostics and Quick Fixes.[/b] Spot configurable source issues as you edit, with targeted fixes where available.
[*][b]Fast offline checks.[/b] Assert diagnostics, symbols, source text, and structure without starting Minecraft or installing Java.
[*][b]Real Paper/Skript execution.[/b] Select your compatible local JARs and run assertions in disposable server environments.
[*][b]Evidence you can inspect.[/b] Review individual assertions, source diagnostics, console excerpts, and observed runtime versions.
[*][b]Native Test Explorer.[/b] Discover tests, run selections, rerun failures, and cancel execution from familiar VS Code controls.
[*][b]Saved run history.[/b] Revisit earlier results and compare runs with the same test selection.
[*][b]Reports for your workflow.[/b] Export JSON, HTML, or JUnit results for investigation and sharing.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Your dashboard, your style[/b][/size]

Choose [b]White[/b], [b]Dark[/b], or [b]Follow VS Code[/b]. Your appearance choice is remembered.

Search, filter, and sort results; expand assertion details; inspect runtime readiness; and follow trends for comparable test selections. Passing, failing, skipped, cancelled, and errored outcomes stay distinct, so incomplete runs do not become a misleading green result.

